-- Explanation of the counterexample:
-- Q1 will output an empty set because for c1='1' from t3, alias2.c2 'Y' is in t6 causing NOT EXISTS clause to be false.
-- Q2 will output '1' because there exists a match across all involved tables that satisfies the conditions of the EXISTS clause.

